  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The Kota of the Nilgiri hills play instrumental music led by the kol, a double-reed shawm, with drums including the tabatk frame drum and the dobar, and kob horns, at funerals, the annual god ceremony and other festivals; a repertoire of god tunes is tied to particular ritual moments. Richard K. Wolf's fieldwork documents it in detail. The kuzhal card stands in for the kol, the frame-drum card for the tabatk and the generic drum for the dobar.",
